[ALLGEMEIN]
XFDisk Help
===========

Keyboard
--------

Use the cursor keys to select a
partition or a free area.

Use the Enter or Return key to
open the menu corresponding to the
selected area.

Press the F3 key to exit the FDISK
program.

Use the Tab key to switch between
multiple hard drives.


Display
-------

The meaning of the individual ele-
ments of the display is:

Name   Position and name of the
       partition in the boot menu.
       The default partition is
       marked with '0'.

Dr     Drive Drive letter under DOS
       and OS/2.

Status  Status of the partition:
        ACTIVE  primary partition
                from which the sys-
                tem boots by de-
                fault.
        INACTIVE primary partition
        N/A     logical drive
        FREE    free area

Type    Type of partition (primary
        partition or logical drive
        in an extended partition).

Size    Partition size in MB (1 MB =
        1024 KB, 1 KB = 1024 B).

System  File system used on the
        partition (e.g., FAT)

Label   Label of the partition that
        is entered during format-
        ting.


Boot Manager
------------

The boot manager allows you to in-
stall multiple operating systems on
one hard drive and start them from
a menu that is displayed every time
you start the computer.

The boot manager is installed on
the first cylinder of the hard
disk, which is usually unused for
technical reasons.

The boot manager is therefore not
compatible with programs that also
use this area, such as Disk Manager
for managing hard drives larger
than 512 MB.

WARNING: If you install the boot
manager and use a disk manager that
also uses this area, you may lose
data irretrievably.


Warranty Notice
---------------

Use XFDisk at your own risk! We
assume no liability for data loss,
damage to hardware, software, or
anything else, nor for any resul-
ting consequential damages or
failures.

Be sure to back up your valuable
data before using this program.


Freeware Notice
---------------

This program is freeware and may
therefore be freely copied.
Please read XFDISK.TXT for more in-
formation.
[ENDKEY]
